export const OFFICE_MANUAL_COMMON_FULL_TEXT: string = "# KRAVIA OFFICE\n## Common employee user manual\n### From invitation to everyday work, security, approvals and offboarding\n\n**Edition:** 1.0 | **Audit reference:** GitHub `vamsimarripudi/kraviaprivatelimited`, `main` at `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e` (13 November 2026)  \n**Audience:** Invited users, employees, directors, authorized advisers, managers, interns and trainees  \n**Read this first:** This is a **source-code-audited guide**, not a claim that all functions have passed live production verification. Buttons and records may be hidden by assigned permissions, effective dates, deployment configuration, or approval state. No emails are sent by this manual.\n\n> **Rule:** A job title is not a permission. Your Office role, the active scoped access profile, department authority, multifactor authentication (MFA), and server-side approvals determine what you can actually do.\n\n## 01 | Quick orientation: which site, which identity?\n\n**Official company sign-in:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com/office/login`. The site’s sign-in component specifically instructs staff to use the `www` company domain. Check the lock icon and exact address before entering credentials. **Do not** treat `/join` as an employee-registration route: `/join` is for public resources. Office invitation-only registration uses `/office/register?invite=...`, issued privately by an authorized administrator.\n\n- **Office personal dashboard:** `/office/dashboard` — start here when you have Office access.\n- **Your verified employment profile:** `/office/my-role` — role, onboarding evidence, personal details and verified payment record.\n- **Finance workspace:** `/finance/dashboard` — only with an authorized Finance, CA, auditor, director or owner role and applicable capabilities. The Finance-only identity may not have an Office dashboard unless Office access is separately granted.\n- **Account and security:** `/office/settings`; Finance users may have `/finance/settings`.\n- **Personal requests and approvals:** `/office/requests` and `/office/approvals`. A title alone does not let you approve a request.\n\n**What Office does:** It is the private company workspace for assigned work, workforce intake, workflow decisions, documents, HR, engineering, customers, Finance, governance and operations. **What it does not do by itself:** A registration does not confirm employment, a submitted request does not grant authority, a draft salary slip does not prove bank payment, and an uploaded document is not automatically a valid signature.\n\n## 02 | Important differences: invitation, identity, employment and authority\n\n| Item | Meaning | Who controls it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Private invitation | Permission to create an Office identity, time-limited and assigned to an email | Owner / authorized access administrator |\n| Registered account | Credentials were created, email verification completed | The invited person; first-party identity service |\n| MFA-approved session | Password plus approved second factor, and device approval when required | The employee and controlled security reviewers |\n| Active workspace | Office workspace status is `ACTIVE`; processing screens may appear before this | Access governance |\n| Employee onboarding | HR/personal forms, certificates, policy acknowledgement, signed appointment evidence and independent reviews | Employee, HR, Finance, authorized reviewer |\n| Role package | Primary job, additional duties, scoped access and checklist version | Owner / accepted department head within scope |\n| Permanent employee ID | Issued only after employment and required evidence are independently verified | HR and authorized reviewers; guarded database workflow |\n| Payment | Financial ledger, payslip, reviewed settlement and bank evidence | Independent Payroll / Finance controls |\n\n**Typical account states:** `INVITED` means the private invitation still needs acceptance; `REQUESTED` or `PENDING` means review/activation is outstanding; `ACTIVE` means identity/workspace admission; `SUSPENDED` or `REVOKED` means access is not permitted. A user may be registered but still shown `/office/processing` while waiting for workspace activation. Never use a colleague’s account as a workaround.\n\n## 03 | Before your first sign-in: new invitee checklist\n\n1. Confirm the invitation came from KRAVIA’s authorized internal onboarding process. Do not follow unsolicited or forwarded links.\n2. Keep your **registered corporate email** accessible. Your invitation and OTP flows are tied to that identity. A company administrator must resolve incorrect addresses.\n3. Open the **private invitation link** supplied to you. Its destination is `/office/register?invite=...`. Do not type a random token or use the public `/office/register` page.\n4. Check the displayed **full name, corporate email, and assigned role**. Your invitation may carry an initial department/role, but that does not replace a signed appointment or role-package approval.\n5. Enter your full name, then create and confirm a password. Registration validation requires **at least 12 characters, uppercase, lowercase, digit and symbol**. Use a unique password and a trusted password manager.\n6. Select **Complete registration**. Complete the **six-digit corporate-email verification** when prompted (the registration code is shown as expiring after 10 minutes). If necessary use **Send another code**, then verify.\n7. Continue to **KRAVIA Authenticator** activation; registration itself is not full Office access.\n8. Wait for required **phone authorization, new-browser trust and workspace activation**. If the account shows `Processing`, do not create a new registration.\n9. If the invitation is invalid, expired, revoked or already used, ask the person who invited you to reissue it. Do not share invitation tokens in tickets, chats or screenshots.\n10. After successful entry, immediately open **My roles & onboarding** to begin the employee intake checklist. Your appointment and signed documents remain independent.\n\n**Already employed and previously registered?** Do not re-register. Use `/office/login` with the existing credentials and your approved second factor. **External CA, CS (Company Secretary), legal or audit adviser?** Use only the invitation and scoped role assigned to your professional identity; do not request a normal employee record unless HR has explicitly created one.\n\n## 04 | Install and activate KRAVIA Authenticator\n\n**Instructions:** `/office/authenticator`. **Official Android listing:** `https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.kraviaprivatelimited.authenticator`.\n\n1. On an approved Android device, open the Google Play listing shown on the Authenticator page. Do not install APKs sent through email or chat.\n2. Secure your phone with a lock screen, biometric protection and automatic date/time.\n3. Open KRAVIA Authenticator. Follow the app’s corporate sign-in process and use the six-digit code sent to the registered email for **device activation**.\n4. Wait for the verified Owner or authorized administrator to approve **that precise phone**. Device enrollment is protected; the website is not expected to expose a secret QR/setup seed for enrollment.\n5. Once active, obtain the current locally generated six-digit code in the app. Return to `/office/login` to complete browser sign-in.\n6. An iPhone distribution link appears only if KRAVIA has configured an approved Apple channel. The Android Google Play link is not an iOS installer.\n\n**Lost/replaced device:** Stop using the old device; request a governed **Reset MFA** from Office administration. Never copy an old device secret, request another person’s code, or leave the office signed in on a shared device.\n\n## 05 | Sign in, email OTP, QR approval and new-device checks\n\n1. Go to `/office/login`. Enter corporate email and password and select **Sign in to KRAVIA Office**. Finance-authorized users may also have `/finance/login`.\n2. When prompted **Verify your identity**, enter the latest six-digit Authenticator code and select **Verify and continue**. Watch the timer; use a new code after expiry.\n3. **Only if enabled for your account:** select **Send a code to my corporate email instead**. Enter the code on the **Check your corporate email** screen and select **Verify email and enter Office**. The source UI specifies a ten-minute code and a resend option after 60 seconds. An option appearing in code does not prove your mail provider will deliver it in production.\n4. **Alternative:** select **Use Authenticator approval instead**. Scan the one-time browser QR using the trusted KRAVIA Authenticator phone, verify the browser details and explicitly **Accept** or **Reject** on the phone. Do not scan the QR in a third-party app. A QR can expire; restart the request if needed.\n5. **New browser or device:** the screen may say **Approve this browser from your email**. Review the registered-email trust decision; only the original browser can complete that pending request. Never approve an unfamiliar device.\n6. After verified MFA and approved device policy, your authorized workspace opens. If it shows `/office/processing`, the workspace has not been activated; contact an administrator.\n7. To end a session, use the **Sign out** icon in the Office rail. Never simply close a tab on a borrowed computer.\n\n**Password recovery:** `/office/recover`. The primary recovery screen directs staff to an authorized Office administrator for a private controlled link; `/office/reset-password` works only with a valid admin-issued token. The Access administration UI also contains an **Email password reset** control, but delivery depends on actual mail service readiness. Founder recovery is separate and not delegated through routine password support. Never paste reset links into public tickets.\n\n## 06 | Navigate the Office: desktop and mobile\n\n**Desktop layout:** The floating icon rail sits at the left. Select a category (My work, People, Engineering, Commercial, Operations, Finance, Governance, Administration). An expanded secondary menu shows **group headings** and the **actual pages available to your identity**. Choose the page label; the top **breadcrumb** returns to the dashboard. The rail offers **Settings**, workspace switching when allowed, light/dark theme, and **Sign out**.\n\n**Mobile layout:** Select **Open Office menu** (menu icon). Choose a category, expand its subgroup, tap a route, then close the menu. Some dialogs and forms scroll vertically. Use the main content area after the menu is closed; if a floating panel blocks a field, close the panel and reopen it after returning to the top of the content.\n\n**Utilities:** Use **More workspace tools** in the top corner for your presence/attendance status, command search, settings and theme actions. The command menu can also be opened with **Ctrl+K** (or **Cmd+K**) where supported. Browser back returns to the previous screen, but never assume a form has autosaved unless the app shows an explicit success state.\n\n**Why a page is missing:** Navigation filters by role and capability. Even a direct URL may display **“This module is not assigned to your current authority.”** That is intentional. Request the smallest required permission through `/office/requests`; only an administrator or competent department head can grant access. Do not ask an employee to forward private screenshots or export data.\n\n## 07 | First-day profile: My roles & onboarding\n\n**Go to:** `/office/my-role`. In the header, inspect your **name, job title, primary department, employment status** and whether a verified permanent employee ID exists.\n\n1. Expand **Responsibilities & work pattern**. Confirm your primary position, any additional duties, reported work pattern, and scope of authority. If anything is wrong, raise a request rather than silently changing it.\n2. Expand **Onboarding evidence**. Each required task may appear `PENDING`, `SUBMITTED`, `VERIFIED` or `RETURNED`. Only an authorized reviewer can verify evidence; employees cannot verify their own task.\n3. Expand **Personal details, education, bank and signed onboarding · Expand**, then **Employee intake details**.\n4. Enter **full legal name, preferred name, contact phone, date of birth and address** accurately. Add actual education entries, qualifications, institutes, completion dates, professional experience and emergency contacts where applicable.\n5. Complete **tax declaration** fields only with truthful information. For bank details, use the protected form; the account is encrypted server-side if correctly configured and the UI later displays only its last four digits. If the page says encryption is unavailable, stop and contact HR/IT; do not send bank details by email.\n6. Under **Signed appointment & policies**, enter the **document evidence reference** issued by the controlled document process. A typed reference is **not** a signature. Review and acknowledge the applicable policy text before checking the acknowledgement box.\n7. Select **Save private draft**. Only after saving can you upload **profile photo** (JPEG/PNG/WebP, up to 2 MB) and education **certificate PDF** (up to 10 MB). The private scanner and storage service must succeed; uploaded evidence is still pending verification.\n8. Select **Submit complete onboarding for HR review** when the record is complete. Your intake is now read-only until HR verifies it or returns it for corrections.\n9. If HR returns it (`RETURNED`), read the reviewer’s note, correct the missing or inaccurate fields, save, and resubmit. Do not use a second duplicate identity.\n10. HR verifies personal and signature evidence; independent Finance verifies masked bank evidence. The permanent employee ID is issued only after required legal/start-date/checklist gates. The UI may show an **employee ID mail** state; `PENDING` is not proof of an email being delivered.\n11. Expand **Salary slips & verified payment evidence** to inspect available records; if a slip exists, use its PDF link. An issued slip is not a bank credit confirmation.\n\n**Privacy boundary:** Never put a full bank account, PAN, Aadhaar, identity scan, raw signature, recovery token or authenticator secret into an Office task description, public support case, email subject or screenshot.\n\n## 08 | Your daily routine: begin, work, review, finish\n\n**At actual work start:** Open **More workspace tools → My status → Attendance**. Select the actual **Work mode**, then **Check in**. A successful Office login is not attendance. Update your **availability** separately (for example, focused/busy/available according to the displayed options). Set an automatic status expiry if appropriate.\n\n**During work:** Use **Start break** before an unpaid break and **End break** when you return. Work from `/office/tasks` and `/office/requests`; review `/office/notifications` and `/office/calendar` for assigned items. If you can approve something, read the evidence and conflict rules first.\n\n**At work end:** Select **Check out**. Open `/office/worktime` to review daily net hours, your week total, recorded historical entries, candidate overtime and salary-slip ledger. The intended schedule is six **net** hours on Monday–Friday (30 net weekly); start/end times are flexible. The attendance policy’s effective operational tracking date is **14 November 2026**. Historic evidence can be reviewed back to **1 August 2026**, but no past hours should be entered without supporting evidence. Optional weekend or weekday excess hours are **potential**, not approved overtime pay.\n\n**If an attendance entry is wrong:** Do not invent a six-hour default. Capture the real IST start/end, unpaid break, original source reference and explanation; use `/office/worktime` correction workflow only if allowed, or raise an HR request. A submitter or beneficiary cannot approve their own correction. Missing check-in alone is not automatic proof of absence.\n\n## 09 | How to create and track a request\n\n**Go to:** `/office/requests` (or **My work → Requests**). This is the general cross-department **workflow** mechanism, not a chat message.\n\n1. Select **New request**. A side drawer labeled **Create request** opens.\n2. Open **Request type** and search the available governed workflow types. Select the correct category (people/access/engineering/finance/legal/operations/product/customer, as listed for your profile).\n3. Enter a specific **Request title** (what must happen), **Description** (business purpose, expected result, deadline, and non-secret evidence reference), and optional **Resource type** / scoped resource key.\n4. Choose **Priority**: Low, Normal, High or Urgent. Do not use Urgent to bypass approval. Check the workflow preview and target.\n5. Select **Submit into workflow**. Submission creates an approval chain; it does not itself issue money, employment, access, a contract or a production deployment.\n6. In **My requests / Recent workflow**, open the request to view status and the **Approval timeline**. Common states include Draft, Pending, In review, Approved, Rejected, Fulfilled, Cancelled and Expired.\n7. Respond to evidence requests with appropriate controlled references. If a request stalls, identify the assigned reviewer; do not ask another person to bypass the chain.\n\n**Examples:** asking for repo access, an employment document, new hardware, a budget increase, a purchase, or a legal review. Enter only work-related information; sensitive personal evidence belongs in its specialized private area.\n\n## 10 | Tasks, approvals and notifications are different\n\n**Tasks:** `/office/tasks` → **Company inbox**. Tasks are actionable execution work, not legal authority. Open a task, use **Start** to begin and the shown status actions to **Block / Unblock / Complete** as appropriate. Provide an explanation when blocked, and link to the required original evidence. If you have assignment authority, **Create task**, select assignee, enter title/description/task type, priority and department, then confirm. Do not mark done unless the deliverable exists.\n\n**Approvals:** `/office/approvals` → **Your approval queue**. Open the assigned request, review business purpose, evidence, conflicts, prior steps and your actual delegated authority. Record the explicit approval/rejection decision and note. Do not approve your own request, a beneficiary’s salary, a payment you prepared or a department action you no longer own. A user may have a manager title and still lack approval rights.\n\n**Notifications:** `/office/notifications` → search signals and select **Read** or dismiss where available. A read/dismiss action acknowledges viewing the notification; it does not approve the underlying request or satisfy policy acknowledgement. Follow the linked request/task to perform the actual action.\n\n**Calendar:** `/office/calendar` shows authorized events, assigned tasks and selected deadlines. Confirm the event’s source before treating it as a committed legal or statutory deadline; do not record confidential content in a widely visible company event.\n\n## 11 | Company knowledge, policies, documents and legal evidence\n\n**Read policies:** `/office/knowledge` → switch between **Policies**, **Announcements**, and **Knowledge**. Search for the relevant policy, SOP or company announcement. Review the **published version** and complete any explicit acknowledgement. Do not interpret “read notification” as acknowledgement. Only approved editors can create drafts, versions and publish content.\n\n**Secure documents:** `/office/documents` → tabs **Documents / Templates / Clauses / Outputs** (if your profile permits). Find the record and its current version. Draft or create an instance only when authorized; approval, rendering, a signature event and delivery are separate audit stages. Generated PDF/DOCX/HTML/XLSX output does not replace the authoritative structured document record. A signature must be backed by valid signed evidence and review; do not manually mark “signed” merely because a PDF was uploaded.\n\n**Contracts:** `/office/contracts` → follow counterparties, effective/expiry dates, owner, obligations and independently reviewed signed evidence. Signing authority must be delegated and valid; neither a Sales role nor a draft contract grants the right to bind the company.\n\n**Company Secretary:** `/office/governance` covers agenda, board meetings, minutes, resolutions, actions and secretarial follow-up; `CS` here means **Company Secretary**, not Customer Support.\n\n## 12 | How to ask for help or escalate a problem\n\n| Problem | Open this path | What to provide (non-sensitive) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Sign-in, MFA, device, email, software, VPN, laptop | `/office/it` → Service desk | Error time, system, device type, safe screenshot, impact and callback method |\n| Missing capability or wrong role | `/office/requests` → access request, or `/office/access` by authorized admin | Required task, department/resource, least-privilege business reason |\n| Incomplete invitation or registration | Authorized inviter’s `/office/access` invitation ledger | Corporate email, approximate issue date, high-level error; never the invite token |\n| Onboarding personal-data correction | `/office/my-role`; HR reviews `/office/people` | Field to correct and official evidence reference, not raw identity scans in chat |\n| Salary/attendance discrepancy | `/office/worktime`; HR/payroll request if needed | Real dates, approved work evidence, relevant payslip code |\n| Customer case or refund matter | `/office/support` when support role assigned | Case reference, product, customer scope and remedy approval requirement |\n| Work execution blocked | `/office/tasks` or `/office/requests` | Task/request ID, blocker and required decision |\n| Confidential ethical concern | `/office/ethics` if available | Minimum necessary facts via confidential case channel, not ordinary team chat |\n| Privacy/security incident | `/office/privacy`, `/office/security`, or IT service route as permitted | Risk, time, affected resource and minimal non-secret reproduction |\n\n**Important distinction:** `/office/it` is an **internal IT ticket/licensing** workspace; `/office/support` is a **customer support/case** workspace; `/office/requests` is the enterprise approval engine; `/office/tasks` is the execution queue. A unified corporate chat/ticket-escalation inbox discussed for future Office releases is **not verified as live** in the audited main-branch route map.\n\n## 13 | Personal preferences, security and account lifecycle\n\nOpen `/office/settings` → **Account**, **Appearance**, **Security & devices**, and **Communications**. Review your verified identity; select **Light** or **Dark** for workspace appearance. Use **Security & devices** to inspect your own protection and sessions, if presented. Avoid shared browser sessions. Keep device OS updated and use authenticated company equipment.\n\n**Temporary leave/transfer:** Manager/HR should use the governed workforce/request processes and correct effective dates. Do not silently share an old role or customer list. **Department handover** is `/office/department-ownership`: a proposal is not an accepted transfer; only the actual recipient can accept with MFA. After acceptance, former owner write and approval privileges may be permanently restricted, even if that person is the Founder. This is separate from job-title and access-profile edits.\n\n**Offboarding:** Authorized HR/Owner uses `/office/people` and the formal workforce lifecycle (approval, asset return, data custody, access revocation and evidence). Employee should return devices, clear entrusted assets using approved channels, transfer active tasks, resolve corporate documents, and sign out. Never export customer or employee data to personal storage. Revocation is a distinct control; it should not be inferred from last day or payroll status alone.\n\n## 14 | What you will see when something is pending\n\n| Label | Interpretation | What the employee does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `DRAFT` | Entered but not submitted for approval | Finish and explicitly save/submit |\n| `PENDING` / `IN_REVIEW` | In a reviewer’s queue | Monitor request; do not perform the protected action |\n| `SUBMITTED` (intake) | Employee record is under independent review | Wait for reviewer action; correct only when returned |\n| `RETURNED` | Reviewer requested corrections | Read reason, edit and resubmit |\n| `VERIFIED` | Relevant reviewer accepted this evidence | Check subsequent approvals; not equivalent to paid/signed |\n| `APPROVED` | Specified workflow stage approved | Follow execution instructions; not proof of provider action |\n| `FULFILLED` / `DONE` | Execution work completed according to recorded evidence | Verify actual deliverable and linked record |\n| `REJECTED` / `DECLINED` | A specific request or trust decision failed | Read reason and restart through legitimate workflow |\n| `SUSPENDED` / `REVOKED` | Access disabled | Contact authorized admin; do not bypass |\n| `UNKNOWN` / `PENDING` mail | Delivery evidence is missing, queued or uncertain | Do not assume the email was received |\n| `COMPLIANT` / `FILED` | Should be used only with actual external evidence and professional review | Validate the relevant filing/evidence source |\n\n## 15 | Troubleshooting: the ten most frequent cases\n\n1. **Invite link invalid:** Return to the inviter; request a new link from `/office/access`. Do not copy a token into a ticket.\n2. **Password accepted but no dashboard:** Complete MFA, new-browser approval or workspace processing. If denied, do not repeat registration.\n3. **No email OTP:** Check registered email and Spam; use the permitted resend after the UI’s interval. If no provider acknowledgement, use Authenticator if available or ask authorized admin to investigate mail delivery. The code being shown as “sent” in the frontend is not an independent SMTP proof.\n4. **Authenticator code rejected:** Enable automatic phone time, enter the current unexpired code, verify the correct phone. Never ask for another person’s OTP.\n5. **New-device trust blocked:** Verify the exact browser request and registered-email action; reject unknown devices.\n6. **Settings or module not visible:** It may require capability assignment; use an access request rather than a direct URL workaround.\n7. **A control is greyed out:** The action may need reviewer scope, `ACTIVE` identity, effective start date, verified evidence, or deployment dependency. Save what is available and raise an appropriately scoped request.\n8. **Personal/bank profile cannot save:** Check the current draft state and privacy/encryption warning. Never substitute email or unsupported file shares.\n9. **Attendance not updating:** Confirm **Check in** occurred, breaks were ended, and **Check out** succeeded. An app login is not a working session.\n10. **Document/payroll status seems final but external action did not occur:** Verify provider acknowledgement, bank settlement, signed artifact and the separate reviewer/evidence references.\n\n## 16 | Security and professional conduct: non-negotiable controls\n\n- Only use your assigned account and authorized equipment. Never share password, MFA code, recovery token or unapproved QR screenshot.\n- Use **least privilege**: request only the permission and resource scope required for a specific duty; review/revoke when duty ends.\n- Never self-approve any high-risk action, salary change, financial settlement, disciplinary outcome, corporate appointment or transfer of company authority.\n- Store identity documents, bank and signature records only in their dedicated private Office workflows. Respect data minimization and retention controls.\n- A company professional (CA, Company Secretary, legal adviser or auditor) signs off only within their formal competence and engagement. Office status is not a substitute for external filings or legal approval.\n- Treat machine-generated summaries and AI recommendations as **advice requiring human verification**. Use only approved AI tools and scoped data.\n- Report suspected phishing, leak, unauthorized access, lost device or unusual login promptly through the appropriate restricted channel.\n\n## 17 | First week checklist\n\n- [ ] Accepted valid private invitation or used previously registered identity.\n- [ ] Registered/verified corporate email; completed MFA and device trust.\n- [ ] Opened the correct Office or Finance dashboard; checked own role/profile.\n- [ ] Completed personal onboarding draft, required documents and applicable policy acknowledgements.\n- [ ] Submitted required onboarding evidence; checked reviewer status, no false `VERIFIED` claim.\n- [ ] Reviewed tasks, requests, notifications and company calendar.\n- [ ] Practised a legitimate workflow request without using sensitive data in descriptions.\n- [ ] Used explicit Check in / Break / Check out on each actual workday after the effective date.\n- [ ] Confirmed who reviews work, who manages IT access, and which escalation channel applies.\n- [ ] Verified profile's permanent ID and payslip only when independently issued.\n\n## 18 | Source verification and limits of this edition\n\nReviewed `main` contains route registries for **54 Office subsections** and **21 Finance subsections**, a permission-filtered floating-rail shell, the invitation/registration and MFA components, employee intake and role packages, Company Inbox, request/approval workflows, HR worktime, and operational modules. This establishes **code-level existence**, not full live availability. I could not verify authenticated production behavior, database migration application, provider-delivered invitations/OTPs, every UI interaction or actual audit logs. The connected Vercel workspace did not expose a matching KRAVIA project during this review. Treat the versioned source links listed in the master manual as the technical reference; refresh screenshots and labels against a real non-production test identity before mass distribution.\n\n**Not verified as shipped:** A dedicated `/office/info` manual sidebar/personal acknowledgment module; a unified employee-to-employee corporate chat/group/mention interface; automatic delivery of role-specific PDF attachments on invitation. These are described in the separate rollout specification, not represented here as working controls.";
export const OFFICE_MANUAL_ROLES_FULL_TEXT: string = "# KRAVIA OFFICE\n## Role-by-role employee operating guides\n### From Founder / Owner through Trainee\n\n**26 distinct onboarding guides**, source-audited at `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`. To build a ready-to-send new-joiner PDF, the distribution bundle places the Common Guide before the relevant role guide. This section can also be served to signed-in users based on their canonical role-package assignment.\n\n| Order | Role / work profile | Appendix ID |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 01 | Founder / Owner | `01_FOUNDER_OWNER` |\n| 02 | Board Director / CEO | `02_BOARD_DIRECTOR_CEO` |\n| 03 | COO / Chief Operating Officer | `03_COO_OPERATIONS_HEAD` |\n| 04 | CFO / Finance Head | `04_CFO_FINANCE_HEAD` |\n| 05 | CTO / Chief Technology Officer | `05_CTO_ENGINEERING_HEAD` |\n| 06 | CDO / Data or Digital Head | `06_CDO_DATA_HEAD` |\n| 07 | Head Administrator / Access Administrator | `07_HEAD_ADMIN_ACCESS` |\n| 08 | Company Secretary (CS) | `08_COMPANY_SECRETARY` |\n| 09 | Chartered Accountant (CA) / Tax Adviser | `09_CHARTERED_ACCOUNTANT` |\n| 10 | Legal Counsel / Contract Manager | `10_LEGAL_COUNSEL` |\n| 11 | HR Manager / Head of People | `11_HR_PEOPLE_MANAGER` |\n| 12 | Department Head / Line Manager | `12_DEPARTMENT_MANAGER` |\n| 13 | Engineering Manager / Technical Lead | `13_ENGINEERING_TEAM_LEAD` |\n| 14 | Full Stack Developer / Software Engineer | `14_FULL_STACK_DEVELOPER` |\n| 15 | Product Manager / Product Administrator | `15_PRODUCT_MANAGER` |\n| 16 | Sales / Business Development / Marketing | `16_SALES_CRM_MARKETING` |\n| 17 | Customer Support / Service Case Agent | `17_CUSTOMER_SUPPORT` |\n| 18 | Finance Analyst / Payroll Specialist | `18_FINANCE_ANALYST_PAYROLL` |\n| 19 | Recruiter / People Operations Coordinator | `19_RECRUITER_PEOPLE_OPS` |\n| 20 | Procurement / Facilities / Operations Staff | `20_PROCUREMENT_FACILITIES` |\n| 21 | IT Service / Security Administrator | `21_IT_SECURITY_ADMINISTRATOR` |\n| 22 | Quality / Compliance / Risk Lead | `22_QUALITY_COMPLIANCE_RISK` |\n| 23 | Independent Auditor / Assurance Reviewer | `23_INDEPENDENT_AUDITOR` |\n| 24 | General Employee / Office Member | `24_GENERAL_EMPLOYEE` |\n| 25 | Intern / Graduate Intern | `25_INTERN` |\n| 26 | Trainee / New Joiner | `26_TRAINEE` |\n\n**Role selection rule:** the role assigned through the employee’s effective primary position and supplemental functional duties should select the manual, but the shown routes must further be filtered by real permissions. Trainee and intern are employment relationships, not Office technical roles. \n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Founder / Owner\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nCompany-wide governance, delegated access, strategy, selected technical oversight and lawful authority decisions; retain separation between oversight and execution.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`OWNER` is a protected technical role. Do not treat Founder authority as permission to circumvent Finance, statutory appointment, department handover or independent approvals.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/my-role` | Role package, private onboarding, signed evidence and personal record |\n| `/office/access` | Controlled invitations, role changes and security/access review |\n| `/office/role-packages` | Authorized staff create draft package, publish version and assign to verified employee |\n| `/office/department-ownership` | Current owner proposes transfer |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/decisions` | Review scoped risks, change requests and recorded decisions |\n| `/office/strategy` | Open strategy cycle and objectives |\n| `/office/intelligence` | Read executive brief and exception summaries |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/readiness` | Read operational readiness signals and failed controls |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n| `/office/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Open `/office/dashboard` to review assigned work and exception summaries.\n2. Confirm your identity, approved device and current scoped rights at `/office/settings`.\n3. Review `/office/role-packages` and `/office/access` to understand active staff and delegated authority\n4. do not create synthetic records.\n5. Open `/office/approvals` to identify pending decisions requiring an independent reviewer.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Review decisions and risks in `/office/decisions`, goals in `/office/strategy`, and project exceptions in `/office/portfolio`.\n2. Use `/office/access` to approve legitimate roles, device/MFA requests, and access reviews with a reason.\n3. Confirm ownership proposals in `/office/department-ownership` do not take effect until the recipient accepts.\n4. Review audit evidence before closing a sensitive transaction\n5. ensure the receiving department retains authority after transfer.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a department lead needs ongoing authority: verify their identity and role; review current ownership; propose the appropriate transfer in `/office/department-ownership`; have the recipient independently accept in their own MFA session; then check audit and read/write restrictions. Do not accept on their behalf.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nOwner-approved business decision with recorded reason, proper checker, current department ownership and an audit trail, not a silent permission override.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNo employee approval of their own compensation, no fabricated signatures, no payment from a draft, no second Owner by routine admin actions. Founder view can be read-only after ownership transfer.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor blocked executive decisions use `/office/requests`; for IT/security incidents use `/office/it` where assigned and escalate to the current accountable professional. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Board Director / CEO\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nExecute approved corporate strategy and lead management through the applicable director, executive and department-scoped permissions.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nCommon Office base role may include `DIRECTOR`; CEO is a job title, not a special Office login role or blanket operational power.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/manager` | Read team/direct-report queue |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/strategy` | Open strategy cycle and objectives |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/governance` | Open meeting/agenda, prepare minutes or resolution where authorized, then route for proper secretarial approvals. |\n| `/office/decisions` | Review scoped risks, change requests and recorded decisions |\n| `/office/compliance` | Review applicability and obligations |\n| `/office/contracts` | Open agreement, check counterparty, dates and obligations |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check the identity and position displayed at `/office/my-role` when Office access permits.\n2. Read current corporate policies and announcements at `/office/knowledge`.\n3. Inspect strategy, board/decision tasks and assigned approval queue.\n4. Confirm which departments are managed directly and which have a distinct owner.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Review executive KPIs and human-reported progress in `/office/strategy` and `/office/portfolio`.\n2. Assign team work through the Company Inbox or Manager workspace when an established reporting line allows it.\n3. Record board-resolution and governance evidence through the authorized process.\n4. Review only decisions that appear in your actual `/office/approvals` queue.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a board action is required: find the agenda and supporting material in `/office/governance`; check the decision or obligation; direct an authorized Company Secretary to prepare minutes and signed evidence; review the resolution within its workflow; verify the final governed record before operational execution.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nRecorded executive decisions, visible follow-up owners and supporting signed resolutions where legally required.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nDirector or CEO does not imply authority to approve own employment terms, use private HR data, execute bank transfers or bypass a departmental handover.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nEscalate unresolved statutory matters to Company Secretary/Legal; use `/office/requests` for cross-department action and `/office/approvals` for authorized decisions. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · COO / Chief Operating Officer\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nCoordinate day-to-day service delivery, operating controls, vendor work, assets, facilities and team-level execution.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nCOO is a title; access commonly requires `OPERATIONS`, `DIRECTOR` or `MEMBER` plus procurement, facilities, asset and relevant department capabilities.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/manager` | Read team/direct-report queue |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/vendors` | Open vendor or purchase case |\n| `/office/assets` | Search approved asset registry, issue/return/transfer workflow and evidence of custody or disposal. |\n| `/office/facilities` | View rooms, visitors and facilities issues |\n| `/office/travel` | Create governed travel request or claim with policy and supporting receipts |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/resilience` | Open continuity plan/test or incident |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm assigned Operations department, reporting line and working pattern in your Office profile.\n2. Examine open work, SLAs and blocked items in `/office/tasks`.\n3. Open `/office/vendors` and `/office/assets` to learn the active registered vendors and equipment.\n4. Check the approval boundary for procurement and high-risk exceptions.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Prioritize deadlines and assign legitimate team tasks.\n2. Review purchase requests, receipts and asset custody before escalating spend.\n3. Check facilities issues, travel needs, quality nonconformances and continuity risks.\n4. Hand off completed operational evidence to Finance/Legal where their independent approval is required.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a team needs a laptop: create a governed request in `/office/requests`; obtain applicable purchase authorization; track vendor quotes/PO in `/office/vendors`; record receipt in the controlled workflow; assign the physical asset in `/office/assets`; keep invoice and payment actions separate.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nEquipment and supplier workflow with approval, PO/receipt, employee assignment, vendor provenance and closed operational task.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nOperations approvals are not banking approvals. Supplier entry is not proof of payment or delivery. Department authority must be current.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nOpen `/office/it` for technical outages if authorized; use `/office/requests` for Finance/Legal decisions and `/office/quality` for defects. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · CFO / Finance Head\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nOversee revenue, treasury, budgets, statutory finance review, payroll and financial reporting with segregation of duties.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nFinance access requires `FINANCE`, `DIRECTOR` or separately assigned finance capability. CFO title alone does not confer payout or filing authority.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/finance/dashboard` | Review finance command-center and current exceptions |\n| `/finance/billing` | Open invoice/customer |\n| `/finance/payroll` | Review approved payroll calculation/batch, prepare payout instructions where delegated |\n| `/finance/budget` | Open budget cycle, review commitments and actuals, propose controlled adjustment. |\n| `/finance/gst` | Review invoice-derived GST working register, period status and filing artifacts |\n| `/finance/accounting` | Review double-entry trial balance and period lock |\n| `/finance/banking` | Open masked bank account/transaction source |\n| `/finance/payments` | Prepare payout instruction, route independent approval, inspect provider mode, and separately confirm execution. |\n| `/finance/expenses` | Enter company obligation/claim, select lawful funding mode and attach evidence |\n| `/finance/reconciliation` | Open transactions, inspect auto-match proposals and manually handle ambiguous/unmatched records. |\n| `/finance/compliance` | Open tax/accounting obligations and inspection evidence |\n| `/finance/audit` | Review inspection packs and permitted tamper-evident records |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Enter `/finance/login` if assigned to Finance and verify MFA.\n2. Confirm current books, active accounting period and currency in `/finance/dashboard`.\n3. Review company bank reference, payment provider readiness, approver separation and period lock status.\n4. Understand each finance action’s documented source record and authorized reviewer.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Review billing versus receipts and aging.\n2. Review budgets and expenses without approving your own requests.\n3. Monitor bank imports, unmatched transactions and independent reconciliations.\n4. Confirm payroll batches and GST evidence, with no inference that portal filing or bank settlement occurred.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a vendor payment is needed: verify the approved purchase/invoice evidence; stage a payment instruction in `/finance/payments` only if permitted; obtain independent approval; confirm actual provider/bank result and reconcile; keep a traceable source reference. A staged instruction is not money transferred.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nBalanced, auditable records; clear approval separation; source-backed tax evidence and verified settlement.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNever infer GST filing, tax liability, bank-side transfer or salary paid from an internal draft status. Company funds and ownership ledger are distinct.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor mismatched books open `/finance/reconciliation`; for tax opinions request authorized CA review; for suspicious payments escalate to the Owner and security authority. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · CTO / Chief Technology Officer\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nGovern company technology, release quality, incidents, providers, technical assets and change management.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nCTO is a title; the protected Owner/Director or properly assigned engineering permissions determine read/write access. Production deployment is governed.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/engineering` | Open your assigned service/repository |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/products` | Search canonical product registry |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/security` | Review permission-scoped security dashboard, changes and security intake |\n| `/office/devices` | Review trusted identity/device posture, corporate badges or physical access where assigned |\n| `/office/it` | Select Service desk or Licences |\n| `/office/integrations` | View approved embed/integration registration |\n| `/office/domains` | Review domain/certificate inventory and expiry |\n| `/office/ai` | Review approved tools and permitted use-case scope |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check your assigned projects, repositories and source-of-truth systems.\n2. Review access and device posture in `/office/security` and `/office/devices` if permitted.\n3. Inspect engineering workstreams and on-call ownership at `/office/engineering`.\n4. Review release expectations and quality evidence.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Triage incidents, deployments and service health in `/office/engineering`.\n2. Create/assign team tasks and record change approvals.\n3. Cross-check security exposure, domains/certificates and approved integrations.\n4. Close a release only after verified CI, appropriate change approval, deployment and operational checks.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a release is proposed: link it to a project or change request; review tests and security checks; require a human approver where configured; observe the actual deployment; attach commit, build and service evidence; then mark the operational task complete.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nTraceable change with commit/release reference, tests, authorization, production fingerprint and incident rollback owner.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nDo not assume a Git merge is a production deployment or that a code-based capability exists on the live DB. Avoid secrets in tickets and screenshots.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor access issues route to `/office/access` through an admin or create an access request; log incidents through the assigned engineering/IT workflows. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · CDO / Data or Digital Head\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nControl data ownership, lawful sharing, import/export, privacy and approved AI use.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nCDO is a title, not an OfficeRole. Requires explicit `data.*`, `privacy.*` and scoped read/write capabilities.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/data` | Create governed export/import/movement request |\n| `/office/privacy` | Open privacy case/retention control, classify exposure and follow restricted resolution. |\n| `/office/ai` | Review approved tools and permitted use-case scope |\n| `/office/trust` | Review approved vendor/customer assurance requests and controlled supporting evidence. |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Identify data custodians and approved purposes.\n2. Review access scopes before handling employee, customer or vendor information.\n3. Read privacy rules in `/office/knowledge` and assigned records in `/office/privacy`.\n4. Check what data-movement operations and approvals are enabled for your profile.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Review proposed exports, imports and AI use cases.\n2. Request authority for new movement rather than copying data into messages.\n3. Track retention concerns, vendor assurance and incident evidence.\n4. Record actions and reviewer decisions for sensitive changes.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a project needs a data export: open `/office/data` or create an appropriate request; record source, purpose, scope and recipient; obtain configured independent approval; use the approved delivery path; verify audit events and retention rules.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nApproved, minimum-necessary data transfer with immutable reason, authorization and custody evidence.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nData title cannot bypass user consent, row-level security, confidential ethics restrictions or a departmental authority transfer.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nSecurity event -> `/office/it` or Security authority; data subject matter -> `/office/privacy`; new approval -> `/office/requests`. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Head Administrator / Access Administrator\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nManage authorized invitations, staff identity, role grants, department assignments, device trust and access lifecycle.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nProtected access roles `ADMIN` and `OWNER`; Head Admin is an organizational title and must be mapped to a real scoped profile. ADMIN does not become an OWNER.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/access` | Controlled invitations, role changes and security/access review |\n| `/office/role-packages` | Authorized staff create draft package, publish version and assign to verified employee |\n| `/office/department-ownership` | Current owner proposes transfer |\n| `/office/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n| `/office/devices` | Review trusted identity/device posture, corporate badges or physical access where assigned |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Open `/office/access` using AAL2 and confirm your allowed administrative scope.\n2. Learn how to issue single-use invitations, review onboarding ledger and resolve incorrect email addresses.\n3. Review current delegated permissions and temporary role expiry.\n4. Verify sensitive Owner/Director transitions are reserved for the correct authority.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Issue invitations only for approved hires or professional access with correct email, department and role.\n2. Review pending activation/device decisions and record reasons.\n3. Revoke or suspend leavers as directed by approved offboarding.\n4. Reconcile access and audit entries without sharing tokens or passwords.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a newly approved staff member: verify accepted offer or appointment evidence; choose `Invite an employee` in `/office/access`; enter email, name, job title, department, roles and business reason; privately provide the generated invitation; monitor their registered and MFA status; grant scoped job access only after required approval.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nActivated identity linked to an approved role, department, effective date and audit trail, without unapproved escalation.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nDo not share invitation URLs publicly, grant a second Owner, bypass protected identity recovery, or convert a title to implicit permissions.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor OTP/provider failures investigate the official delivery and worker state, then route to authorized platform support; use controlled recovery rather than credentials by email. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Company Secretary (CS)\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nMaintain corporate governance, meeting records, board resolutions, statutory registers and professional review evidence.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`CS` in KRAVIA means **Company Secretary**, not Customer Support. Appointment/qualification and permitted authority must be valid independently.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/governance` | Open meeting/agenda, prepare minutes or resolution where authorized, then route for proper secretarial approvals. |\n| `/office/compliance` | Review applicability and obligations |\n| `/office/registrations` | Review company registration type, masked identifier and renewal schedule |\n| `/office/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/office/decisions` | Review scoped risks, change requests and recorded decisions |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm appointment and professional authority before entering statutory actions.\n2. Read current registers, document templates and board calendar.\n3. Check the case owner and supporting documents for upcoming meeting records.\n4. Understand the independent director/authority signature process.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Prepare agendas, board packs, minutes and resolution records.\n2. Maintain due-date and registration evidence.\n3. Route agreements and resolutions through authorized reviewers and signing processes.\n4. Record actual filing/acknowledgment evidence only after external confirmation.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a board resolution: create or open the meeting in `/office/governance`; attach agenda and reference materials; prepare the decision/minutes in a controlled record; seek authorized approval/signatures; add verified signed version in `/office/documents`; only then mark related obligations satisfied.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nComplete corporate record with meeting date, version, signers, professional review and applicable filing evidence.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nOffice record preparation is not legal execution or MCA filing. CS authority and signatory powers are not inferred from technical `CS` login alone.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nEscalate formal legal interpretation to Legal counsel and reserved corporate approvals to Board/Owner; log unanswered actions as governed requests. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Chartered Accountant (CA) / Tax Adviser\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nPrepare, review and reconcile company finance and tax records; provide independent professional verification.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`CA` may land in Finance workspace. Professional appointment and valid consent govern access to client records; CA cannot self-approve or assume executive powers.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/finance/dashboard` | Review finance command-center and current exceptions |\n| `/finance/accounting` | Review double-entry trial balance and period lock |\n| `/finance/gst` | Review invoice-derived GST working register, period status and filing artifacts |\n| `/finance/reconciliation` | Open transactions, inspect auto-match proposals and manually handle ambiguous/unmatched records. |\n| `/finance/billing` | Open invoice/customer |\n| `/finance/compliance` | Open tax/accounting obligations and inspection evidence |\n| `/finance/audit` | Review inspection packs and permitted tamper-evident records |\n| `/finance/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/finance/banking` | Open masked bank account/transaction source |\n| `/finance/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Sign into `/finance/login` using assigned professional credentials.\n2. Review authorized entity, period and supporting ledger/counterparty records.\n3. Check GST data provenance and whether integration/portal filing is externally confirmed.\n4. Identify independent approval responsibilities and masked bank fields.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Reconcile books and evidence prior to tax conclusions.\n2. Review draft GST workings and flag missing invoice/ITC data.\n3. Request source docs for unresolved records.\n4. Document professional review without claiming portal filing before receipt.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a GST-period review: open `/finance/gst`; compare issued invoices with `/finance/billing` and ledger; inspect exceptions; record proposed adjustments; require permitted approval; retain portal acknowledgment or actual filing evidence separately.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nReconciled tax working papers and source-backed professional opinion, not inferred compliance.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNever fabricate input credits, bank transactions, tax receipts, digital signatures or filing confirmation. Protected private data stays within approved scope.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nEscalate unresolved tax interpretations to the appointed CA signatory/Finance head; use controlled requests for missing evidence. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Legal Counsel / Contract Manager\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nPrepare, review and track agreements, obligations, signatures and legal-risk decisions.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`LEGAL` technical role plus `legal.*`, document and governance permissions as assigned; professional authority requires separate appointment.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/contracts` | Open agreement, check counterparty, dates and obligations |\n| `/office/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/office/governance` | Open meeting/agenda, prepare minutes or resolution where authorized, then route for proper secretarial approvals. |\n| `/office/decisions` | Review scoped risks, change requests and recorded decisions |\n| `/office/compliance` | Review applicability and obligations |\n| `/office/registrations` | Review company registration type, masked identifier and renewal schedule |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Read active contract templates, privacy rules and approval matrix.\n2. Identify authorized signatories and execution channels.\n3. Inspect assigned legal cases or obligations.\n4. Verify there are no private signing keys in editable text.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Review counterparties, legal terms, renewal dates and owners.\n2. Prepare versioned drafts in `/office/documents` or `/office/contracts` according to the workflow.\n3. Request independent approval, e-sign or verified signed evidence.\n4. Update obligations only when documentation supports a status change.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor an agreement: inspect the counterparty and intended purpose; prepare a controlled draft; route for approval; receive independently verified signature/e-sign evidence; register executed version and obligations; remind accountable owners before expiry.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nExecuted document with verifiable signatory, immutable versions, review history and obligation owner.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nA typed reference, file upload or unchecked provider label is not itself valid e-signing. Do not publish privileged content.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nContract dispute to legal head/board; technical document issue to IT; access issue through workflow. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · HR Manager / Head of People\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nRecruit people, independently verify employee onboarding, maintain workforce records, attendance corrections and offboarding.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nExpected `HR` with scoped People, onboarding and payroll review permissions. A planned HR assignment is not effective until its dated identity/MFA gates pass.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/recruitment` | Open requisition/candidate |\n| `/office/people` | Open scoped workforce directory |\n| `/office/role-packages` | Authorized staff create draft package, publish version and assign to verified employee |\n| `/office/worktime` | Recorded working hours, breaks, monthly evidence and payslips |\n| `/office/payroll` | Open salary components/pay period |\n| `/office/manager` | Read team/direct-report queue |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Review employee privacy, approved recruitment requisitions and latest onboarding queue.\n2. Open `/office/people` → `HR employee intake & verification desk` for authorized profiles.\n3. Confirm current effective date and salary policy instead of making assumptions.\n4. Identify independent Finance bank-verification and signed appointment evidence requirements.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Advance candidate status only against legitimate HR evidence.\n2. Review employee submitted intake and return incomplete records with a precise reason.\n3. Examine attendance claims and seek independent reviewer for corrections.\n4. Coordinate approved joiner/leaver workflow and asset return, without claiming payment execution.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a new employee: track requisition/offer in `/office/recruitment`; arrange approved invitation; obtain self-entry at `/office/my-role`; review private HR evidence; require Finance bank verification and signed appointment task; verify onboarding; issue permanent ID only when all guards allow.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nEmployee onboarding state VERIFIED and permanent ID only after signed and verified evidence; no raw bank number disclosure.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nHR cannot approve its own worktime claim, invent historical hours, make legal appointments or assert that salary paid from a payroll draft.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nRefer unresolved bank verification to Finance; invitation or MFA to authorized Access admin; discrepancies in employment evidence to Legal/Owner. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Department Head / Line Manager\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nOwn team assignments, review delegated requests, supervise workload and maintain departmental controls.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nManager access derives from a real reporting line, accepted department ownership and scoped profiles; neither `MEMBER` nor managerial title alone grants access.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/manager` | Read team/direct-report queue |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/department-ownership` | Current owner proposes transfer |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/development` | Open assigned skills/training/performance |\n| `/office/calendar` | Open an authorized event or deadline |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check that your team appears correctly in `/office/manager`.\n2. Review role package and departmental jurisdiction.\n3. Read policy updates and recurring team meeting calendar.\n4. Identify what decisions are assigned to you and which require Finance/Owner review.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Assign only direct-report tasks and check blockers.\n2. Review request evidence and approve only queued steps with valid authority.\n3. Track training, progress and objectives without fabricated performance ratings.\n4. Keep ownership handover logs and former-owner restrictions intact.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen an employee requests access: inspect request type/scope in `/office/requests`; verify need and current team; act only if `/office/approvals` assigns you that step; refer privilege grants to `/office/access` administrator; verify the employee receives actual capability.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nAssigned employee receives only approved scoped access and the decision remains auditable.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNo manager may approve a self-originated or self-benefiting claim. An assigned role package is not a statutory appointment or payroll authorization.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor cross-department blockage create a request; for employee support route to IT or HR using the proper case type. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Engineering Manager / Technical Lead\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nLead development execution, service reliability, release reviews, incident responses and engineering onboarding.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nUsually Office `MEMBER`/`OPERATIONS` with engineering, portfolio and repository-scoped permissions; no automatic environment access.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/engineering` | Open your assigned service/repository |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/it` | Select Service desk or Licences |\n| `/office/domains` | Review domain/certificate inventory and expiry |\n| `/office/devices` | Review trusted identity/device posture, corporate badges or physical access where assigned |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm assigned project/repository scopes and applicable CI environment.\n2. Review active incidents, on-call plan and current releases.\n3. Inspect each developer’s tasks and blockers, not unassigned financial/private records.\n4. Learn the team’s code review and emergency change policy.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Triage issues and assign implementable tasks.\n2. Coordinate verified CI/testing before release submission.\n3. Record service/incident evidence and corrective action.\n4. Request extra secrets/devices through authorized access paths.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a production bug: open service case at `/office/engineering`; create traceable task in `/office/tasks`; identify repo and commit; review test proof; submit governed change request and approval; verify deployment health; close only after confirming externally.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nIssue with owner, reproduction, fix reference, test result, approval and release observation.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nApproval of a code review is not approval of finance, secret release or customer data access; keep deploy execution strictly scoped.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nEscalate critical security impact to authorized security owner and record an incident; vendor/network issues to IT. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Full Stack Developer / Software Engineer\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nImplement assigned frontend/backend work, support incident fixes, document evidence and protect source/data access.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`MEMBER` or another Office role plus explicit engineering/project/repo permissions; frontend/full-stack title confers no automatic CTO authority.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/engineering` | Open your assigned service/repository |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/it` | Select Service desk or Licences |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n| `/office/worktime` | Recorded working hours, breaks, monthly evidence and payslips |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Open `/office/my-role` and verify your team, project and onboarding tasks.\n2. Read engineering standards, code/data rules at `/office/knowledge`.\n3. Check assigned tasks at `/office/tasks` and project milestones at `/office/portfolio`.\n4. Set availability\n5. check in using the actual attendance control before work begins.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Start your task, reproduce the issue, code within assigned repository, test and add evidence.\n2. When blocked mark task blocked with a meaningful reason\n3. ask via `/office/requests` or your manager.\n4. Attach PR/commit/test references to task and request review\n5. avoid claiming deployed until observed.\n6. Log real breaks and checkout, then verify `/office/worktime`.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a feature: open task; confirm acceptance criteria; create code changes in approved repo; run tests; request review; follow authorized CI/release process; record SHA, test result and deployment if it occurred; mark task completed with evidence.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nTrackable task with tested change, linked evidence and explicit reviewer/production status.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\nNever expose secrets in screenshots, reuse another employee’s permissions, bypass approvals, or treat a merged PR as live.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nSubmit IT ticket for device/token failures; create a governed request for access or blocked cross-team action. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Product Manager / Product Administrator\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nMaintain product catalog, roadmap, release requests, customer context and measurable portfolio milestones.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`PRODUCT_ADMIN` may access relevant product/portfolio modules with additional scoped capabilities. Product Admin role is not blanket Finance/HR authority.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/products` | Search canonical product registry |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/customers` | Look up canonical customer |\n| `/office/crm` | Open leads/opportunities |\n| `/office/strategy` | Open strategy cycle and objectives |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check assigned product(s), owners and published roadmap.\n2. Review authoritative customer and product names, not invented entries.\n3. Learn the product release and approval boundary.\n4. Open active backlog tasks and user-reported quality issues.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Reconcile customer needs with planned milestones.\n2. Draft updates and request permitted product approvals.\n3. Coordinate with Engineering, Sales and Support without exposing finance totals outside scope.\n4. Monitor completion by evidence rather than passive task activity.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a release milestone: open product/portfolio record; create acceptance criteria and dependencies; assign engineering delivery task; attach test/support evidence; submit product release approval if required; verify actual deployment and update the milestone.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nProduct release with named approver, deliverable scope, artifact links and truthful live status.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nCreating a product record does not permit issuing invoices, accessing restricted customer data or shipping production code.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nMarket need to Sales CRM; defects to Engineering/Quality; delegated rights to approved access administrator. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Sales / Business Development / Marketing\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nQualify leads, maintain customer/prospect records and coordinate contracting/invoicing without bypassing legal controls.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nOffice `MEMBER`, `OPERATIONS` or `PRODUCT_ADMIN` with `sales.crm.*` scope; MARKETING is a business function, not necessarily a distinct technical role.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/crm` | Open leads/opportunities |\n| `/office/customers` | Look up canonical customer |\n| `/office/products` | Search canonical product registry |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Read approved company/product descriptions and customer-communication policy.\n2. Verify assigned territory, CRM scope and lead status definitions.\n3. Open CRM queue and understand source/consent data capture.\n4. Confirm who is authorized to prepare legal contracts and commercial terms.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Create/update only legitimately sourced leads and opportunities.\n2. Record factual next action, owner and customer communication date.\n3. Request pricing or contract deviations through the approval workflow.\n4. Hand off accepted deal to Legal/Finance and confirm invoice only via canonical billing record.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor an opportunity: create a lead in `/office/crm`; qualify need and next action; associate permitted customer/product; obtain quote/contract approval; hand off to `/office/contracts` or authorized billing owner; log follow-up and close reason.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nCustomer pipeline with provenance, consent where applicable, approved terms and finance handoff reference.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nCRM stage WON is not proof of signed agreement, invoice, money received or customer data consent. Do not claim unapproved partner credentials.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nCustomer issue to Support operations; invoice questions to Finance; legal terms to authorized Legal reviewer. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Customer Support / Service Case Agent\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nIntake, triage, track and resolve customer support cases with permitted remedy/refund escalation.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nCustomer Support is written in full to avoid confusion with `CS` (Company Secretary). Access requires a scoped `support.case.*` profile and an allowed Office base role.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/support` | Customer support case management, escalation and remedy evidence |\n| `/office/customers` | Look up canonical customer |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/it` | Select Service desk or Licences |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Read approved support scripts, escalation policy, customer privacy rules and service levels.\n2. Confirm what customers/products you are assigned to see.\n3. Open `/office/support` and familiarize yourself with case status, priority and owner.\n4. Identify independent refund/credit approvers.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Open or update a support case with factual description, owner and source.\n2. Request technical help through Engineering or IT without duplicating private data.\n3. Escalate refund/remedy as a governed request rather than promising money.\n4. Confirm customer-facing outcome before marking a case resolved.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nWhen a user reports a fault: find/create the customer case in `/office/support`; classify priority; assign the accountable owner; link permitted technical task; communicate approved progress; verify fix; record resolution and customer confirmation.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nCase trail containing intake source, allowed customer fields, response, triage owner and verified resolution.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nCustomer Support cannot unilaterally approve bank refunds, change product entitlements without authorization or access restricted HR records.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nIncident to Engineering/IT; privacy grievance to Privacy; refund/finance to Finance approver through a request. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Finance Analyst / Payroll Specialist\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nPrepare accurate period records, payroll calculations, expense and reconciliation evidence under independent checker controls.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nExpected `FINANCE` technical role or scoped finance/payroll profiles. Finance-only user may be redirected away from `/office/my-role`; request an authorized onboarding view rather than guessing access.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/finance/dashboard` | Review finance command-center and current exceptions |\n| `/finance/billing` | Open invoice/customer |\n| `/finance/payroll` | Review approved payroll calculation/batch, prepare payout instructions where delegated |\n| `/finance/accounting` | Review double-entry trial balance and period lock |\n| `/finance/banking` | Open masked bank account/transaction source |\n| `/finance/reconciliation` | Open transactions, inspect auto-match proposals and manually handle ambiguous/unmatched records. |\n| `/finance/payments` | Prepare payout instruction, route independent approval, inspect provider mode, and separately confirm execution. |\n| `/finance/expenses` | Enter company obligation/claim, select lawful funding mode and attach evidence |\n| `/finance/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/finance/audit` | Review inspection packs and permitted tamper-evident records |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm actual employer, pay period, currency and authorized role.\n2. Read approved salary rules and documented employee records.\n3. Verify bank masked details are source-backed and not entered into tickets.\n4. Check maker/checker ownership and period lock.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Prepare payroll calculations from approved attendance and pay policy, not raw login times.\n2. Reconcile receipts/expenses and identify unresolved entries.\n3. Stage but do not approve self-originated payment actions.\n4. Archive salary slips and payment evidence separately.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor monthly payroll: verify HR effective employment dates and authorized compensation; inspect approved worktime; prepare calculations at `/finance/payroll`; request independent review; issue payslip via authorized workflow; confirm external bank settlement and reconcile.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nLocked payroll result, payslip reference, approval trail and actual settlement evidence.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nPreparing a payroll batch does not authorize or prove a bank disbursement. Overtime candidates need explicit approved policy.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nAttendance disputes to HR; salary policy to Finance head/Owner; bank feed exceptions to reconciliation owner. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Recruiter / People Operations Coordinator\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nHandle staffing requisitions, candidate pipeline, interviews, offer preparation and approved pre-onboarding.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nNeeds assigned `HR` and `hiring.*` capabilities; recruitment access is narrower than full employee-record or compensation access.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/recruitment` | Open requisition/candidate |\n| `/office/people` | Open scoped workforce directory |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/calendar` | Open an authorized event or deadline |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm which hiring requisitions and departments are approved.\n2. Read candidate privacy/confidentiality rules.\n3. Learn the headcount/offer approval path.\n4. Check who issues invitations and verifies signed appointment evidence.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Add candidate records from authorized sources, schedule interviews and record factual status.\n2. Draft offer only from approved compensation envelope and templates.\n3. Submit offer and pre-onboarding requests for necessary review.\n4. Transfer accepted candidate to HR verification rather than declaring employment complete.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a candidate: confirm approved requisition; add applicant; record interviews and outcome; prepare an authorized offer; get independent approval; record acceptance evidence; request Office invitation; track HR intake and role package tasks separately.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nCandidate pipeline with legal offer evidence, controlled access request and tracked onboarding task.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nA candidate created in ATS is not an employee; an issued offer is not accepted or signed unless real evidence exists.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nCompensation exception to Owner/Finance, legal terms to Legal, new identity to Access admin. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Procurement / Facilities / Operations Staff\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nCoordinate vendors, purchase orders, receipt evidence, corporate assets, rooms, visitors and maintenance.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nExpected `OPERATIONS` or `MEMBER` with relevant scoped vendor/asset/facilities capabilities.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/vendors` | Open vendor or purchase case |\n| `/office/assets` | Search approved asset registry, issue/return/transfer workflow and evidence of custody or disposal. |\n| `/office/facilities` | View rooms, visitors and facilities issues |\n| `/office/travel` | Create governed travel request or claim with policy and supporting receipts |\n| `/office/cards` | Open assigned card/spend request |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check approved vendor list and PO limits.\n2. Inspect asset/room booking permissions.\n3. Understand approval and receipt confirmation roles.\n4. Read safety and security requirements for visitors and company property.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Prepare purchase requests with quotes and scope.\n2. Track approved PO delivery and record receipt only after physical confirmation.\n3. Maintain asset custodian, location and return records.\n4. Log facilities issues and visitor access according to policy.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor office supplies: request purchase; attach quote; obtain approvals; issue PO if authorized; verify goods receipt; update vendor and inventory; transfer invoice evidence for independent Finance payment.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nApproved purchase with vendor source, receipt, asset or facility record, and finance handoff.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nOperational receipt is not Finance payout; do not store card PAN/CVV or visitor IDs in public notes.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nSafety issue to authorized facilities/security owner; vendor invoice payment to Finance; device incident to IT. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · IT Service / Security Administrator\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nManage scoped technology service tickets, approved licenses, device posture, security incidents and identity hygiene.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\nNeeds explicit `it.*`, `identity.*`, `security.*` and possibly `access.*` rights. IT support does not automatically mean access administration.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/it` | Select Service desk or Licences |\n| `/office/devices` | Review trusted identity/device posture, corporate badges or physical access where assigned |\n| `/office/security` | Review permission-scoped security dashboard, changes and security intake |\n| `/office/access` | Controlled invitations, role changes and security/access review |\n| `/office/integrations` | View approved embed/integration registration |\n| `/office/domains` | Review domain/certificate inventory and expiry |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/resilience` | Open continuity plan/test or incident |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Check current service desk, device and certificate state.\n2. Verify which identity actions require Owner/ADMIN approval and independent recovery.\n3. Review incident severity handling and log retention.\n4. Understand secrets and scanned-file policy.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Triage service desk tickets\n2. record owner, severity and resolution.\n3. Provision/revoke approved licenses and devices with auditable custody.\n4. Investigate unusual MFA/device events without asking users to disclose secrets.\n5. Verify production monitoring/certificate changes using external evidence, not only UI.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a lost work phone: record incident in `/office/it`; block or revoke trusted device through an authorized process; request governed MFA reset from Access admin; confirm reactivation on the new phone; document actions with times.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nIncident ticket with affected identity/device, revocation, approval, remediation and post-incident verification.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNever request user passwords/TOTP seeds or silently trust a browser/device. Separation between IT support and privileged Office admin remains mandatory.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nSevere breach to security/Owner, employee HR matters to HR, external provider incident to designated technical owner. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Quality / Compliance / Risk Lead\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nMaintain CAPA, audit readiness, risks, policy applicability and source-backed assurance evidence.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`AUDITOR`, `LEGAL`, `CS` or Office roles with specific `quality.*`, `compliance.*`, `governance.*`/audit rights; actual scope differs by person.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/quality` | Open nonconformance or corrective/preventive action |\n| `/office/compliance` | Review applicability and obligations |\n| `/office/decisions` | Review scoped risks, change requests and recorded decisions |\n| `/office/audit` | Search permitted material activity and trace back to source |\n| `/office/readiness` | Read operational readiness signals and failed controls |\n| `/office/trust` | Review approved vendor/customer assurance requests and controlled supporting evidence. |\n| `/office/resilience` | Open continuity plan/test or incident |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Identify approved standards, policy owners and assurance scope.\n2. Open risk and CAPA records that are explicitly in your authority.\n3. Confirm review evidence needed for closure.\n4. Read confidential-data and audit segregation rules.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Log real nonconformance and root cause, not fabricated metrics.\n2. Assign corrective actions and independently review proof of closure.\n3. Track compliance due dates and actual filing/report evidence.\n4. Escalate unresolved major risks through governed decisions.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a repeated failure: open a quality case in `/office/quality`; document facts and evidence; assign CAPA; obtain reviewer approval; verify action effectiveness; preserve signed/immutable evidence in audit-ready record.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nTraceable nonconformance-to-CAPA chain with root cause, accountable owner, due date and evidence-backed verification.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nAn internal checkbox does not imply a statutory certificate, successful filing, professional audit opinion or real-world process effectiveness.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nSerious risk to Owner/Board; statutory issue to CS/CA; security control issue to security authority. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Independent Auditor / Assurance Reviewer\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nReview authorized evidence and exception trails without taking operational ownership of the area under review.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`AUDITOR` technical role tends toward Finance-only for workspaces; privileged audit trails are restricted by actual permissions and confidentiality.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/finance/dashboard` | Review finance command-center and current exceptions |\n| `/finance/audit` | Review inspection packs and permitted tamper-evident records |\n| `/finance/accounting` | Review double-entry trial balance and period lock |\n| `/finance/reconciliation` | Open transactions, inspect auto-match proposals and manually handle ambiguous/unmatched records. |\n| `/finance/compliance` | Open tax/accounting obligations and inspection evidence |\n| `/finance/documents` | Controlled templates, drafts, signatures and output evidence |\n| `/finance/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Confirm engagement scope and independence before access.\n2. Sign in with independent MFA credentials, not an employee account.\n3. Check period and document provenance.\n4. Identify controls that must be reviewed without mutating.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Read underlying accounting and payment evidence.\n2. Trace samples through the relevant approval/action/settlement chain.\n3. Flag unresolved findings without editing another person’s operational evidence.\n4. Retain report and professional conclusions with authorized distribution.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor sampling a payment: find ledger entry and invoice; inspect approval chain and bank source; compare dates/amounts; record any mismatch as an audit finding; request remediation from the process owner rather than changing records yourself.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nIndependent audit workpaper citing exact records, date, exception and reviewer.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nIndependent Auditor is not the authorizing finance checker for own findings, and does not get universal personal data visibility.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nEscalate material control failures to authorized governance/Board committee; request missing evidence through the process owner. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · General Employee / Office Member\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nUse personal work, requests, calendar, attendance, policies and limited business modules assigned by the manager.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`MEMBER` is a common technical role but business modules still require scoped capability. Some employees have another base Office role.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/my-role` | Role package, private onboarding, signed evidence and personal record |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/approvals` | Human decisions assigned to your current legal / operational authority |\n| `/office/notifications` | Search unread signals |\n| `/office/calendar` | Open an authorized event or deadline |\n| `/office/worktime` | Recorded working hours, breaks, monthly evidence and payslips |\n| `/office/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n| `/office/emergency` | Enter/update your private emergency contact details |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Accept your own invite\n2. activate MFA and ensure the workspace is active.\n3. Complete private onboarding at `/office/my-role` and record genuine signed/evidence references.\n4. Read assigned policy notices and team guidance.\n5. Learn the status/attendance menu and verify it starts from actual check-in.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Check in, then read priority tasks and notifications.\n2. Start/complete assigned work and record proof.\n3. Use Requests for access/equipment/leave/finance or other cross-team needs.\n4. Take break and check out\n5. review hours and pending onboarding items.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor an unavailable tool: open `/office/requests`; choose the appropriate workflow type; describe work purpose and scope; submit; monitor `/office/approvals` status from your request details; begin only when granted capability is actually active.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nAccurate profile, real attendance, traceable assigned tasks, timely requests, no overshared data.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNo job title permits you to approve your own request, see all company data, sign agreements or receive compensation automatically.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nIT ticket for technical issues when assigned; otherwise create a Request or contact authorized supervisor through established channel. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Intern / Graduate Intern\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nLearn workplace standards, perform supervised tasks, track real worktime and provide training evidence.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`INTERN` is an employment type in the role-package catalog, **not** an OfficeRole. Expected technical permissions are narrow and may derive from `MEMBER` plus project scope.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/my-role` | Role package, private onboarding, signed evidence and personal record |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/portfolio` | Open assigned project or workstream |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/notifications` | Search unread signals |\n| `/office/calendar` | Open an authorized event or deadline |\n| `/office/worktime` | Recorded working hours, breaks, monthly evidence and payslips |\n| `/office/knowledge` | Approved policies, internal announcements and SOPs |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Accept the invitation and set up Authenticator personally.\n2. Open `/office/my-role`\n3. confirm internship period, supervisor and onboarding checklist.\n4. Read security, acceptable use, confidentiality and learning policies.\n5. Check whether any repository or client permission has actually been granted.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Check in for actual work and attend scheduled training.\n2. Work only on assigned tasks\n3. ask your mentor before any production-impacting action.\n4. Record code, research or training evidence in the task.\n5. Ask for access or help through the approved workflow, then check out.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFor a first supervised task: open `/office/tasks`; read expected outcome; clarify with mentor; do work in assigned environment; attach meaningful reference; submit for review; wait for verification before marking completed.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nCompleted training item and accepted deliverable, with mentor verification and accurate worktime.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNo production changes, financial approvals, client exports, self-awarded certifications or assumption of regular employee benefits.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nTechnical block to mentor/IT; attendance discrepancy to HR; access requirement through `/office/requests`. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Role guide · Trainee / New Joiner\n\n> **Important:** Read the separate **Common Employee User Manual** first. This role guide is a practical supplement, not a grant of access. A corporate job title does **not** grant technical capabilities, statutory powers, approval rights, or financial authority. Actual buttons and data depend on active identity, MFA, role, assigned profiles, current department ownership, and production readiness.\n\n**Canonical site:** `https://www.kraviaprivatelimited.com`  \n**Edition:** 1.0 · 13 November 2026 · Source-audited at `main` commit `86806c876c5483c18e68c51749e8b2fa7297e60e`  \n**Release verification:** UI source confirmed; live deployment, outbound notifications, integrations, production schema and actual per-user access not independently confirmed.\n\n### Purpose of this role\n\nComplete safe account activation and onboarding, learn the Office basics and perform low-risk supervised work.\n\n### Actual access identity\n\n`TRAINEE` is an employment type, not a technical OfficeRole. Permissions are assigned specifically and should begin at least privilege.\n\n### Routes and where to go\n\n| Open this path | Why it matters in your job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/office/login` | Personal work / controlled record; use only actions offered to you |\n| `/office/authenticator` | Personal work / controlled record; use only actions offered to you |\n| `/office/my-role` | Role package, private onboarding, signed evidence and personal record |\n| `/office/dashboard` | Read your work metrics |\n| `/office/tasks` | Execution tasks, blockers, status and supporting work evidence |\n| `/office/requests` | Submit governed needs, attach business context, track escalation |\n| `/office/notifications` | Search unread signals |\n| `/office/calendar` | Open an authorized event or deadline |\n| `/office/worktime` | Recorded working hours, breaks, monthly evidence and payslips |\n| `/office/settings` | Account, appearance, security, registered devices and preferences |\n\n### First-day / first-access checklist\n\n1. Read the Common Employee Guide before opening any sensitive screen.\n2. Accept your private invitation\n3. create password\n4. verify email\n5. activate Authenticator and trusted device.\n6. Open `/office/my-role` and submit actual personal and signed-onboarding evidence to HR.\n7. Locate the sidebar, dashboard, Settings and Help/Request workflow.\n\n### Daily / recurring operating sequence\n\n1. Check in when you actually begin work.\n2. Read notifications and one assigned training task at a time.\n3. Ask your supervisor for clarification and use requests for any missing access.\n4. Keep a record of completed tasks and real working hours\n5. check out at the end.\n\n### Worked example — from start to completion\n\nFirst task exercise: sign in; open `/office/tasks`; read one assigned training task; confirm it is safe; record progress and evidence; have supervisor check the output; return to dashboard; review onboarding status and sign out.\n\n### What counts as completed\n\nTrainee knows how to enter, find work, request help, protect data, submit actual evidence and leave a secure session.\n\n### Safety and authority boundary\n\nNever use other employee credentials, approve anything not assigned, upload identity scans to chat/email, or enter fake attendance.\n\n### When blocked, denied or uncertain\n\nFor any unfamiliar warning or denied screen, stop and ask the assigned mentor/HR/Access admin through a valid company channel. Always record the actual error, time and affected section without sharing passwords, codes, raw bank details or identity documents. A missing sidebar link may reflect a deliberate permission rule.\n\n### End of day, transfer or employment exit\n\nReview outstanding assigned work in your task/request queues. Hand off context and supporting records to an authorized recipient, complete actual attendance checkout if applicable, and **Sign out**. For offboarding, follow an approved HR/Access workflow; do not simply delete local files or assume a user was deactivated.\n";
